@@ tutor
**Problem 2 · harder**

A disk head is at cylinder 60. Requests are pending for cylinders 95, 12, 70, 48, 130 and 33. Serve them with SSTF (shortest seek time first): the next request served is always the one nearest the head's current position. Find the order of service and the total head movement in cylinders.

<solution>From 60: 70 (10). From 70: 48 (22). Then 33 (15), 12 (21), 95 (83), 130 (35). Order 70, 48, 33, 12, 95, 130. Total 10 + 22 + 15 + 21 + 83 + 35 = 186 cylinders.</solution>
<check lang="python">
pos, left, order, total = 60, [95, 12, 70, 48, 130, 33], [], 0
while left:
    n = min(left, key=lambda c: abs(c - pos))
    total += abs(n - pos)
    pos = n
    left.remove(n)
    order.append(n)
assert order == [70, 48, 33, 12, 95, 130] and total == 186
</check>

<ask type="problem">The order of service and the total head movement, with each move's length.</ask>
@@ learner answer sure
from 60 the closest is 70 (10 away). from 70 the next closest is 95, thats 25. then 130 (35). then back down to 48 which is 82, then 33 (15), then 12 (21). order 70, 95, 130, 48, 33, 12. total = 10+25+35+82+15+21 = 188 cylindres
@@ reply
<grade verdict="partial" score="0.5">The first move is right: "from 60 the closest is 70 (10 away)". The first wrong step is "from 70 the next closest is 95, thats 25": cylinder 48 is only 22 away from 70, so SSTF turns back and serves 48 next.</grade>

SSTF has no direction: at every step it compares all pending requests on both sides of the head. Your later picks and your sum are consistent with having gone to 95, so there is one error, not several. From 70 the correct run is 48 (22), 33 (15), 12 (21), 95 (83), 130 (35), giving the order 70, 48, 33, 12, 95, 130 and a total of 10 + 22 + 15 + 21 + 83 + 35 = 186 cylinders.

<card>SSTF: which request is served next? :: The pending request nearest the head's current position, on either side. Recompute every distance after each move.</card>

<note>SSTF: after each move, measure the distance from the new head position to every pending request, in both directions, and take the smallest.</note>

**Problem 3 · same level**

The head is at cylinder 45. Requests are pending for cylinders 20, 88, 52, 110, 31 and 64. Serve them with SSTF.

<solution>From 45: 52 (7). Then 64 (12), 88 (24), 110 (22), 31 (79), 20 (11). Order 52, 64, 88, 110, 31, 20. Total 7 + 12 + 24 + 22 + 79 + 11 = 155 cylinders.</solution>
<check lang="python">
pos, left, order, total = 45, [20, 88, 52, 110, 31, 64], [], 0
while left:
    n = min(left, key=lambda c: abs(c - pos))
    total += abs(n - pos)
    pos = n
    left.remove(n)
    order.append(n)
assert order == [52, 64, 88, 110, 31, 20] and total == 155
</check>

<ask type="problem">The order of service and the total head movement, with each move's length.</ask>
@@ verify
def sstf(pos, reqs):
    left, order, moves = list(reqs), [], []
    while left:
        d = sorted(abs(c - pos) for c in left)
        assert len(d) == 1 or d[0] != d[1], ('tie', pos)       # no tie at any step
        n = min(left, key=lambda c: abs(c - pos)); moves.append(abs(n - pos)); pos = n; left.remove(n); order.append(n)
    return order, moves
order, moves = sstf(60, [95, 12, 70, 48, 130, 33])
assert order == [70, 48, 33, 12, 95, 130] and moves == [10, 22, 15, 21, 83, 35] and sum(moves) == 186
assert '10 + 22 + 15 + 21 + 83 + 35 = 186' in reply
# the learner's route: one wrong pick at 70, then nearest-first from there
assert abs(95 - 70) == 25 and abs(48 - 70) == 22
o2, m2 = sstf(95, [12, 48, 130, 33])
assert o2 == [130, 48, 33, 12] and m2 == [35, 82, 15, 21] and 10 + 25 + sum(m2) == 188
assert '10+25+35+82+15+21 = 188' in learner
o3, m3 = sstf(45, [20, 88, 52, 110, 31, 64])
assert o3 == [52, 64, 88, 110, 31, 20] and m3 == [7, 12, 24, 22, 79, 11] and sum(m3) == 155
assert '155' in solution(reply) and '155' not in visible(reply)

